meta {
  name: Refresh one post's metrics now
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/posts/:id/analytics/collect
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{postId}}
}

tests {
  test('status is successful', function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200]);
  });
}

docs {
  Re-reads one post from the network instead of waiting for the next scheduled collection, and stores the reading so it joins that post's timeline. `id` is a FoPost post id or, URL-encoded, the permalink of a post made natively on the network. One post is still a platform call, so this spends the same per-user budget as `POST /v1/analytics/collect`: over the limit, the `429` body carries `retryAfter` in seconds. An API key needs the `analytics` scope as well as `posts`.

  Requires the `analytics` scope when using an API key.

  **Scope:** `analytics`
}
